  "query_preview": "..The upper air pattern across the CONUS for much of \nthe next 7 days will be be dominated by trofiness in the west \nand ridging in the east. This trofiness in the west this weekend\nwill bring gusty southwest winds, elevated to critical fire \nweather conditions, drier air, and near normal high temperatures\nto southeast Arizona.\n\nThe main concern for SE AZ this weekend is fire related as the \ngusty winds will combine with low afternoon RH values to produce\ncritical fire weather conditions across most of the forecast \narea. A Red Flag Warnings has been hoisted for most of the area \nthis weekend. The drier air pushing in will limit any chances \n(10-20%) for showers or storms today to the southeast parts of \nCochise county, or southeast of a San Simon to Bisbee line.\n\nNext week will see trofiness in the west slowly weakening thru \nThursday with high pressure building west over the July 4th \nholiday weekend. Afternoon breezes during the first half of next\nweek with elevated fire weather conditions on Monday. Dry next \nweek as we turn the calendar from June to July. Ensembles are \nhinting at a weak push of moisture by the end of next week that \nmay lead to a very low end chance of storms mainly near the \nAZ/NM state line.\n\nThere are hints in the modeled world that the upper high will be\nbuilding toward the 4-corners after July 4th, thus putting the \narea in a favorable monsoon flow which may last through the end\nof July. CPCs 8-14 day precipitation outlook for July 4-10 is \nleaning above normal (35-45% chance). Fingers crossed.",
